From 48eac6c3432949a6532093c814c5def73aa549b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:11:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] macos-arm64: RT capture and composite as queued
 render-thread calls

The capture and composite were screen-space quads with a shader whose draw
pass ran the tracer. Saving a game flushes the material queue on the main
thread for the thumbnail, where the engine's dynamic vertex buffers take a
system-memory path that does not survive the unlock through togl: every
manual or auto save crashed with ray tracing on. The client now queues plain
function calls (ICallQueue::QueueCall) at the same points of the frame; the
RayTraceComposite shader is gone. The hooks also only run for the player's
view (save thumbnails and overlay views come through RenderView too).
